Kelvin Chu, UIUC Physics (CHU@UIMRL3.MRL.UIUC.EDU) wrote:
: 1.  I (perhaps stupidly) managed to eat a nymph corpse and now and teleporting
: 	involuntarily all over the bloody dungeon.  How do I stop this?  (or 
: 	must I get a ring of teleport control?)  

You can:
1) Get a gremlin to steal the intrinsic (but he might steal a more
   valuable intrinsic)
2) Wear a ring of teleport control
3) Wait until you get the teleport control at a certain or from a tengu
   (a message will be something like "you feel in control"

: 2.  Do tinned foods just not (um...) hack it; are they particularly low in 
: 	nutritional value?  I found after clearing out a throne room that when
: 	I tinned everything, I just spent time eating _all_ the tins
: 	immediately afterwards (this was before I was the King o' teleport)
: 	because they didn't fill me up.  Do I have some weird intrinsic, or
: 	is this just the case for unblessed tins?  

I think that's the point.  People have trouble eating corpses because
they are worth too much food.  If you want the monsters to be worth some
food AND get thier intrinsic, then don't tin them.  I like to tin certain
creatures in case I lose some intrinsic.  They are light, and don't go
bad.  My best example is a tin of floating eye meat.  Its a good one to
have in case you kill a shopkeeper or a temple priest and the gods take
away the Telepathy intrinsic.

